---
export const prerender = true;

import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";

const page = getAboutPage("kit-qr-onboarding")!;
---
<AboutArticle slug={page.slug} title={page.title} description={page.description}>
  <h2>What to encode</h2>
  <p>
    After creating a push device (Dashboard → Devices), encode the ingest URL:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`https://your-domain/api/ingest/YOUR_DEVICE_KEY`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Anyone scanning the QR on a phone sees the URL — keep devices physically secure; rotate keys if a sticker is lost.
  </p>

  <h2>Generate a QR</h2>
  <p>
    Use any QR generator (or print from your label maker) with the curl test payload from
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/ingest-and-webhooks">Ingest & webhooks</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Onboarding checklist</h2>
  <p>
    The dashboard getting-started card tracks device creation, sensor keys, test POST, and alerts.
    Pair the QR with sensor labels that match firmware keys (<code>temp1</code>, <code>door1</code>, …).
  </p>
</AboutArticle>
